{
  "requirement": "The harness MUST expose:\n\n```text\nfinish_search({ search_id: UUID, used: Array<String> })\n    -> { search_id: UUID, finished: true }\n```\n\nThe arguments MUST contain exactly these fields.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.authoring.finish_search`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. The harness exposes a `finish_search` tool taking `{search_id: UUID, used: Array<String>}`.\n2. The tool returns `{search_id, finished: true}`.\n3. The arguments contain exactly the fields `search_id` and `used`.\n\n**Tool exposure and schema**\n- `src/authoring/tools.rs#mod[tests]/fn[finish_search_advertises_the_accounting_schema_and_selection_rule]` finds `finish_search` in `definitions()`.\n- It asserts the exact `parameters` schema: `search_id` is a string with `format: uuid`, `used` is an array of strings, both are required, and `additionalProperties` is false.\n- This covers the \"exactly these fields\" obligation at the schema level.\n- It also asserts that the description states the result form `{search_id, finished:true}`.\n- A tool call named `finish_search` is routed to `pages.finish_search` in `src/authoring/tools.rs#fn[dispatch_paged]`. Tests in `src/authoring/mod.rs` drive that path through the conversation and count `finish_search` calls in the usage log. Examples are `every_submission_kind_waits_for_all_searches_and_can_recover` and `a_bad_tag_returns_a_recoverable_error_without_closing_the_search`.\n\n**Exact-field enforcement**\n`src/authoring/searches.rs#mod[tests]/fn[invalid_completion_is_atomic_and_can_be_corrected]` runs these argument sets through `finish_search`:\n- `null`, `[]` and `{}`.\n- A missing `used` and a missing `search_id`.\n- An extra field, `extra`.\n\nEach one must fail with \"exactly search_id and used\". The same test also rejects:\n- a non-string `search_id` and a malformed UUID string;\n- an unknown but well-formed UUID;\n- `used` that is null or a string rather than an array;\n- non-string `used` elements;\n- an unknown tag.\n\nAfter each failure it asserts that the search stays outstanding and no inputs are recorded. A valid correction then succeeds.\n\n**Result shape**\n- `src/authoring/searches.rs#mod[tests]/fn[delivered_searches_including_empty_results_need_explicit_completion]` asserts that `finished.result` equals `json!({\"search_id\": ..., \"finished\": true})` exactly. That rules out extra or missing result fields.\n- `src/authoring/searches.rs#mod[tests]/fn[selected_dependencies_keep_the_delivered_hash_and_accumulate_without_reads]` asserts the same result and that it has no `text` field. It also covers the empty `used` and repeated-tag cases.\n\nRefining sub-requirements such as `completion`, `invalid`, `atomicity` and `empty` carry their own tests, and I did not reassess them here. I found no gaps and no applicable `{fixme}`.",
